{"id":"obligations/theory/T38","statement":"For closed real intervals, pairwise nonempty intersections suffice for finite families; this is not a claim about every lattice form. Convex sets in R^d require the hypotheses of Helly and witnesses up to d+1. A three-arc discrete circle and fixed halfplanes distinguish two- and three-member empty meets.","status":"open","references":["test/t38-forms.test.ts","vectors/laws/t38/circle12.json","vectors/laws/t38/halfplanes.json"]}
{"id":"obligations/theory/F2","statement":"On twelve discrete points, five-point arcs starting at 0, 4 and 8 meet in every pair and not jointly. This finite example does not prove the absence of every finite Helly bound.","status":"open","references":["vectors/laws/t38/circle12.json","test/t38-forms.test.ts"]}
{"id":"obligations/theory/F3","statement":"The four seller/buyer/carrier/auditor halfplanes conflict with seller/auditor witness; x>=0,y>=0,x+y<=-1 is pairwise consistent and jointly empty. Fixed nonnegative certificates verify these finite cases only.","status":"open","references":["vectors/laws/t38/halfplanes.json","test/t38-forms.test.ts"]}
{"id":"obligations/theory/F4","statement":"Under the provisional integer domain p divides n and 0<=s<p, RI=log2(n/p)-h(s/p). For n=12,p=4, the controls at s=0,1,2,3 are 1.584962500721156,0.7736843762620231,0.5849625007211561,0.7736843762620231 bits. Halfphase is one bit below inphase. Author domain confirmation and worst-case objective remain open.","status":"open","references":["vectors/laws/t87/phase-controls.json","samples/laws/t87/phase-domain.json","test/measures/t87-phase.test.ts"]}
{"id":"obligations/theory/T87","statement":"The raw absolute-angle criterion is not invariant under adding a full turn: phases 0 and 2pi reinforce. Existing cancels uses cos of the difference. This distinguishes a missing wrapped-distance hypothesis; it does not infer laminarity or a near-phase RI worst-case objective.","status":"open","references":["test/measures/t87-phase.test.ts"]}
{"id":"obligations/theory/F1","statement":"For n=3..7, arithmetic reproduces the provided log2(n)-2+2/n values and Bell squared pair counts. No exhaustive partition enumeration, general optimality proof or independent browser/WebAssembly-origin verification was performed.","status":"open","references":["vectors/laws/f1/finite-arithmetic.json","test/t38-forms.test.ts"]}
{"id":"theory/source/L1","statement":"Folding claims is union in the knowledge order; arrival order never decides.","status":"open","references":["docs/theory-2026-10.md"]}
{"id":"theory/source/L2","statement":"For intervals of a lattice, pairs suffice: every conflict has a witness of two (Helly number 2). Convex forms in\\n   R^d need witnesses up to d+1 (d=2 → 3). Cyclic forms (phase) without a declared cut have no finite Helly number;\\n   with a declared cut, h=2 on arcs not crossing it. Shannon partitions have no finite Helly number.","status":"open","references":["docs/theory-2026-10.md"]}
{"id":"theory/source/L3","statement":"Excluding any value from the maximal coincidence may exclude the truth; keeping the fork is the only correct action.","status":"open","references":["docs/theory-2026-10.md"]}
{"id":"theory/source/L4","statement":"Each entering origin closes bits and spends confidence; the guarantee of the meet is 1 − Σp UNDER DECLARED,\\n   JUSTIFIED failure probabilities p_i; if Σp ≥ 1 the bound is trivial and must be reported as such. Agreement\\n   and copy count do not estimate p.","status":"open","references":["docs/theory-2026-10.md"]}
{"id":"theory/source/L5","statement":"In the Shannon lattice, shared information may have no carrier: at most log₂n − 2 + 2/n bits.","status":"open","references":["docs/theory-2026-10.md"]}
{"id":"theory/source/L6","statement":"Information about the truth is bounded by the structure of causes, not by the number of witnesses; copies do not add.","status":"open","references":["docs/theory-2026-10.md"]}
{"id":"theory/source/L7","statement":"A closed group cannot measure its own reliability: for a cause covering all witnesses, P(unanimity on v) = c/n\\n   for every accuracy q, so q is unidentifiable from inside.","status":"open","references":["docs/theory-2026-10.md"]}
{"id":"theory/source/L8","statement":"Only dissent identifies what origins share; unanimity says nothing. For a partial cause, q is identified iff an\\n   outsider exists with error p ≠ (n−1)/n. Rank-breaking structures: same-set factors, singleton factors,\\n   cycle-covering factors, more factors than pairs.","status":"open","references":["docs/theory-2026-10.md"]}
{"id":"theory/source/L9","statement":"Which parameters can be measured is known before observing, from the pairs matrix of declared causes.","status":"open","references":["docs/theory-2026-10.md"]}
{"id":"theory/source/F1","statement":"Extremal: over n equiprobable states, max RI(x,y) = log₂n − 2 + 2/n, attained only by the path on n+1 vertices\\n   (x groups edges by even endpoint, y by odd). Proof chain: lem-phi (φ(t) ≥ 2(t−1)) → lem-merge → lem-identity →\\n   lem-join → lem-meet → thm-extremal. Enumeration n=3..7: 0.251629, 0.500000, 0.721928, 0.918296, 1.093069;\\n   pair counts 25, 225, 2704, 41209, 769129 (Bell numbers squared → complete).","status":"open","references":["docs/theory-2026-10.md"]}
{"id":"theory/source/F2","statement":"Circle of 12 points, arcs of length 5 starting at 0, 4, 8: every pair meets, the three do not.","status":"open","references":["docs/theory-2026-10.md"]}
{"id":"theory/source/F3","statement":"Half-plane claims x+y≤12 (seller), x≥3 (buyer), y≥2 (carrier), x+y≥14 (auditor): CONFLICT, witness\\n   {seller, auditor}, 2 of 4. Minimal example needing three: x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0, x + y ≤ −1 (pairwise consistent,\\n   jointly empty). Both go in as vectors.","status":"open","references":["docs/theory-2026-10.md"]}
{"id":"theory/source/F4","statement":"Phase: RI = log₂(n/p) − h(s/p) with n states, period p dividing n, shift s with 0 ≤ s < p, h the binary entropy;\\n   worst case is near-phase, not anti-phase. (Author to confirm the domain; until then the vector carries these\\n   hypotheses explicitly.)","status":"open","references":["docs/theory-2026-10.md"]}
{"id":"theory/source/F5","statement":"M/4: with a common cause c of accuracy q, C = log₂n − c·[h(q) + (1−q)·log₂(n−1)]; dissent\\n   d = (1−c)·[1 − (1−p)² − p²/(n−1)]. Sample n=4, c=1/5: one covering factor q=0 → 1.683 bits; {A,B},{A,B} → 1.430;\\n   {A,B},{C,D} → 1.937; triangle {A,B},{B,C},{A,C} → 1.835; q=1/2 → 1.642. Numeric policy: binary64-log2.\\n   Negative sample (each a named refusal): missing q → refuse; 2 witnesses requesting c → unmeasured; 3 binary\\n   witnesses → unmeasured; perfect agreement → no-dissent; copies → same bound; partial governance → unmeasured.\\n   HOW FACTORS GOVERN in duplicated/disjoint/triangle models is NOT fully specified: region stays open (§5).","status":"open","references":["docs/theory-2026-10.md"]}
{"id":"obligations/theory/review/H3","statement":"experiment: one-origin finite structural observation; physical interpretation open.","status":"open","references":["src/laws/laws.bound"]}
{"id":"obligations/theory/review/H5","statement":"experiment: finite structural interpretation inherits H3 experiment core; general physical interpretation remains open.","status":"open","references":["src/laws/laws.bound"]}
